.vitest-cache

# Agent worktrees, which are checkouts rather than content
.claude/worktrees/

# Music somebody added in the editor, when the app was run from source.
#
# `editorAudioDir()` resolves under the configured music folder, but it used to
# be a module level `path.join(AUDIO_ROOT, 'Editor')` evaluated at import, when
# AUDIO_ROOT is still empty, which makes it the relative path `Editor`. Two
# uploaded mp3 files were committed that way. The bug is fixed; this is so a
# stale build or an older checkout cannot do it again.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash, because a bare `Editor/` matches a directory
# of that name at any depth, and `src/renderer/src/components/Editor/` is one.
# Every file already in there is tracked, so nothing disappeared, but a new
# component added to the editor would have been ignored without a word.
/Editor/

# The four package web app this was ported from.
#
# Their source was removed from the repository in 3faa3a0, and the folders that
# were left on disk afterwards, 868 MB of build output and node_modules, are
# gone now too. Recover the source from before that commit if it is ever
# wanted: `git show 3faa3a0^:server/src/...`.
#
# Ignored rather than forgotten, so checking out a commit from before the port
# and coming back cannot quietly re-add them.
client/
server/

# UI redesign mockups, round 1.
#
# Three clickable directions for the 3.x redesign, built as standalone static
# pages against a read-only inventory of the current UI. They are a reference
# for the implementation and not a build input, so nothing in `src/` imports
# from them and they are not shipped.
#
# The chosen direction, Minimalist Dark Studio, is handed off with its own copy
# at `~/Downloads/goodbit-3.0-design-handoff/`, which is where the design
# contract, the annotated defects and the audits live. This folder stays on
# disk as the working reference.
/design-prototypes/

# Release planning documents.
#
# Working notes for a bundled minor release: an orchestrator plan and one
# document per issue, written against the codebase before any of it is built.
# They go stale the moment the code lands and the issues themselves are the
# shared record, so these stay local rather than becoming a second source of
# truth somebody has to keep in step.
.planning/
